> My code uses f(Zi,model="iid") for Z1,Z2,Z3, and the identifier for
> each case I have also included as f("personal_ID",model="iid).
>
> Is it correct to assume the hyper parameters are the precisons for
> Z1,Z2 and Z3? I should not worry bout the personal_ID variable?

the hyperparameters are the precisions, yes.

> However, when I run the model with slight different ordering of
> f(Z1),f(Z2) and f(Z3), the posterior precisions for Z1,Z2,Z3 and the
> personal_ID variables differ greatly.

that should not be. unless you have a confounding with several
solutions?? like if

i=j

then

	f(i) + f(j)

might be different than

	f(j) + f(i)

depending on the ordering, it might go to one of the two modes.

> Is there any rules around the ordering of these within the R code?
> Is my understanding of the posterior precisions correct?
>

yes.

if you have an example, I would like to check.

thx

