Finn,

I think I may have misinterpreted your message when you said: "It can't predict for coordinates not covered in the estimation, so the bru() model needs to include the years you want to predict (as in the components need to contain them, even if the data itself doesn't have observations for them)." Do you mean that I need to have a full data set as with inla() where the outcome variable is all NA for the testing period and all predictors have observed values for both the training and testing periods?

Felipe

